# Line endings, pinned — because committed files in this repository are compared to freshly
# generated ones byte for byte: `docs/reference/cli/*.md`, which `check:docs` re-renders from the
# binaries, and `.claude/skills/board-process/SKILL.md`, which `check:skill` re-generates.
#
# Git's Windows default is `core.autocrlf=true`, which stores LF and checks out CRLF. Those files are
# LF in the index, so without this line a fresh clone on Windows would hand those checks CRLF and
# fail them — while CI, on Linux, stayed green. That failure mode is worth closing at the source
# rather than by teaching each check to normalise: a check that ignores line endings also ignores a
# generator that started emitting the wrong ones.
#
# `text=auto` still lets Git detect and leave binary files alone; there are none today, and this
# keeps that from mattering later. Nothing here needs CRLF: the repository has no `.bat` or `.cmd`.
* text=auto eol=lf
